Turn the bootstrap step marks on by default

kernel_bootstrap_log() and kernel_bootstrap_thread_log() mark every step of
kernel_bootstrap() and of the bootstrap thread (bsd_init, kext loading, the
launchd handoff), but both print only under startup_debug &
STARTUP_DEBUG_VERBOSE, and this port leaves that at zero.

run-251 therefore ends at E16 -- STARTUP_SUB_EARLY_BOOT, the last startup
phase -- with nothing after it, which is the position the panel is missing.
Default the tunable to STARTUP_DEBUG_VERBOSE instead of rewriting the two
helpers: zzz-boot-progress.patch already edits both of them, and one edit to
the tunable cannot fight with it.  A boot argument can still turn it off.
---
diff --git a/osfmk/kern/startup.c b/osfmk/kern/startup.c
index bec97fb..14e7ba5 100644
--- a/osfmk/kern/startup.c
+++ b/osfmk/kern/startup.c
@@ -216,7 +216,16 @@ SECURITY_READ_ONLY_LATE(startup_subsystem_id_t) startup_phase = STARTUP_SUB_NONE
 
 extern int serverperfmode;
 
-TUNABLE(startup_debug_t, startup_debug, "startup_debug", 0);
+/*
+ * nio: the bootstrap marks every step it takes through kernel_bootstrap_log()
+ * and kernel_bootstrap_thread_log(), but both are gated on
+ * startup_debug & STARTUP_DEBUG_VERBOSE and this port never sets it, so
+ * everything after STARTUP_SUB_EARLY_BOOT ran blind -- a boot that died in
+ * bsd_init, kext loading or the launchd handoff left the last marker at E16
+ * and nothing after it.  Default the mask on, so the last line of a photo is
+ * the last step that was reached.
+ */
+TUNABLE(startup_debug_t, startup_debug, "startup_debug", STARTUP_DEBUG_VERBOSE);
 
 static inline void
 kernel_bootstrap_log(const char *message)
